    rdfs:label "Evidence for Bleaching Materials used in Calico Cloth & Calico Printing: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 53"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "BLEACHING POWDER: chloride of lime, made by exposing slaked lime to the action of chlorine, which is used for bleaching linens, calicoes, and paper materials: many thousand tons of it are made annually in the kingdom."@en ;
